                <pb facs="0291" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-07T17:00:00+08:00">October 7, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>90. Following sent to Legation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 7, 3 p.m. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> was fired
                            upon by trench mortars from right bank of river at a point 45 miles this
                            side of Kiukiang this morning. Fire was returned with 450 rounds machine
                            gun ammunition and seven 3-inch shells. <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Panay</hi> turned and passed point of attack twice but there was no
                            hand firing from shore. No casualties on <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Panay.</hi></p>
                        <p>Military authorities continue to announce further advances of central
                            forces in Honan. Americans state Feng Yu-hsiang is definitely abandoning
                            Chengchow.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
